      "## Avoiding common traps",
      "Be wary of fake wallet apps, cloned websites and phishing links, and always type addresses or use verified bookmarks. Check every character of a destination address before confirming, because clipboard-hijacking malware can swap addresses silently. Be cautious about signing smart contract permissions you do not understand, as malicious approvals can drain tokens later.",
      "Treat unsolicited giveaways, airdrops and offers of help from strangers in chat groups as hostile until proven otherwise. If something goes wrong, move remaining funds to a new wallet created on a clean device, document what happened and report to Action Fraud. We offer authorised security reviews and awareness training for individuals and firms who want to strengthen their habits.",
