      "## Legislative developments",
      "The Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 amended the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 and related legislation to provide clearer powers to seize, freeze and forfeit crypto assets that are the proceeds of crime or intended for use in unlawful conduct. Authorities can also act more quickly in certain circumstances, and the Act sets out how seized crypto may be realised and the proceeds applied.",
